{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/555","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/555/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/555/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/555/events","html_url":"https://github.com/open5gs/open5gs/issues/555","id":696031341,"node_id":"MDU6SXNzdWU2OTYwMzEzNDE=","number":555,"title":"Stray PFCP associations - SGWC and SMF","user":{"login":"kbarlee","id":8739983,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3Mzk5ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8739983?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kbarlee","html_url":"https://github.com/kbarlee","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kbarlee/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kbarlee/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kbarlee/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kbarlee/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kbarlee/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kbarlee/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kbarlee/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kbarlee/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kbarlee/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":5,"created_at":"2020-09-08T16:55:02Z","updated_at":"2020-09-09T12:52:46Z","closed_at":"2020-09-09T12:52:46Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Hey Sukchan\r\n\r\nI've just noticed something when running some tests.\r\n\r\nI have an `smf.yaml` with x1 UPF listed\r\n```\r\nupf:\r\n    pfcp:\r\n      - addr: 10.10.0.7 \t# N4 cloudUPF_1\r\n```\r\n- `cloudUPF_1` is PFCP associated, however so is another one, `cloudUPF_2`\r\n- `cloudUPF_2` is _not_ listed in the `smf.yaml` config\r\n- The SMF assigns UEs in round robin mode alternately to the two UPFs\r\n\r\nSo it would seem that the SMF assigns UPFs from a list that are currently PFCP associated, rather than those that are listed in it's own config file? I noticed this because I had not turned on IP forwarding on the second server.\r\n \r\nI've checked, and the same happens with the SGWc. It assigns from a list of associated SGWu, regardless if they are listed in the `sgwc.yaml` config.\r\n\r\nCheers\r\nKenny","closed_by":{"login":"kbarlee","id":8739983,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3Mzk5ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8739983?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kbarlee","html_url":"https://github.com/kbarlee","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kbarlee/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kbarlee/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kbarlee/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kbarlee/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kbarlee/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kbarlee/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kbarlee/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kbarlee/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kbarlee/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/555/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/555/timeline","performed_via_git